{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And Abram said to the king, etc.</b> The reason for his raising his hand is so that it be verified to the king of Sodom that he has no intention of going back on this matter — neither all of it nor part of it." "And his saying <b>if a thread</b> etc. and <b>if I take</b> — for he should have said only ״if I take a thread״ etc. — he intended to say in this manner: <b>I have lifted up</b> etc. <b>if a thread</b> etc. — meaning: it is upon me like a terumah-offering if I have taken a thread and even etc. of the property mentioned in the matter. And he further adds that he will not take in the future from all etc., and this is his saying ״and if I take״ etc." "<b>Further,</b> he may intend to say in this manner: <b>I have lifted up my hand</b> — meaning: I have given the terumah-offering that I am obligated from everything, ״if a thread and even״ etc., that which I am obligated according to the law. And do not say that I am greedy for money and claim what is not mine — ״and if I take from all״ etc. — but not because of permissiveness will I rob the One on High of what I am obligated to give Him, which is the tithe-offering."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:41:16.328261435Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}